  "plan_length_note": "plan_length_m is the horizontal length of that OSM way, WGS84 haversine with radius 6378137 m, rounded to one decimal. It is not a climb and not a structural length. An approach plan_length_m stops at the far node stored in the extract. That node is not a surveyed grade point. None of these plan lengths is the structural span. The agreement says the span length shall be a minimum of 46 m. The EIA says the replacement is about 8 m shorter than the existing bridge. Those two sentences were not combined. Way 25601841 is 60.7 m horizontally. That mapped length is not the new span length.",
  "dropped_note": "G118 is the old span, demolished across 29 December 2022 to 3 January 2023. It is not modeled. No G118 folder was written. The ways below are the bridge-tagged lines the extract stored on the G118 object, including the Valley Line construction ways and the two road carriageways. lrt-tracks.json routes 13 and 14 are the full Valley Line West construction centrelines, about 14.1 km each. They pass the centre. They are not a span length and their node lists are not copied. River-span lengths, the river path width, and the river-pier notes are not copied. Alberta file B055 is the 1954 bridge. Its printed lengths were not used as the new span.",
